                source: "Brief N-4 air drag and wind (docs/briefs/N-4-air-drag-wind.md)",
                description: r#"The brief asks for global linear and quadratic drag with a wind vector in SimSettings; it does not fix the linear law, the units or the defaults. Existing scenes must behave as before."#,
                decision: true,
                options: [
                    (
                        label: "Width-scaled, off by default",
                        caption: r#"F = -(c w + 1/2 rho Cd w |r|) r with r = v - wind and w the projected width across r. New SimSettings fields: air_density (areal kg/m2 over the 1 m world depth, default 1.2 = sea-level air), drag_coefficient Cd (default 0 = off), linear_drag c in N s/m2 (default 0 = off), wind (m/s, default 0). With both terms 0 the pass returns at once, so every existing scene behaves exactly as before. Note the world's default body density is 1 kg/m2, about that of the air: at Cd 1 a 1 m box falls at about 4 m/s, a light, Algodoo-like feel; denser bodies fall faster. Fields are additive with serde defaults: old files load, no format bump; the v8 golden gains the four fields."#,
                    ),
                    (
                        label: "Mass-proportional linear drag",
                        caption: r#"Linear drag as a damping rate (F = -k m r), independent of the shape, and quadratic drag as above. Simpler to tune, but a plate would not fall slower face-on in the linear regime."#,
                    ),
                ],
            ),
