                        caption: r#"F = -rho A g - rho k A (v_c - v_fluid) at the submerged centroid c (v_c includes the spin), plus a torque -rho k A (I/m) w. A body as dense as the fluid, wholly in it, loses speed and spin at the rate k. The drag is capped so one step cannot reverse the motion; the push never is. World gravity is used, not the body's gravity scale (the displaced fluid's weight does not depend on the body)."#,
                    ),
                    (
                        label: "Quadratic drag",
                        caption: r#"Closer to water at speed, but stiffer to integrate and with no clean settle; linear drag damps the bobbing the brief asks for."#,
                    ),
