                title: "What do we do about contour edges that drift past the simplification tolerance?",
                source: "Geometry property tests (docs/briefs/6-2-geometry-proptests.md)",
                description: r#"A property found that simplify_ring tested each dropped vertex only against the chord from the last kept vertex to its next neighbour. A run of dropped vertices could drift: on a capsule, the straight side's edge ran 0.48 m into both caps, 7.5e-4 m inside the curve (tolerance 3.2e-4), and the area came out 0.63 % short."#,
                decision: true,
                options: [
                    (
                        label: "Fix it: test the whole dropped run",
                        caption: r#"A vertex is dropped only while every vertex dropped since the last kept one stays within the tolerance of the new chord. Cost O(run length) per vertex, small at the contour's sample budget. Contours may keep a few more vertices on long gentle curves."#,
                    ),
                    (
                        label: "Record a known limit and widen the tolerance",
                        caption: r#"No change to contours, but the error is unbounded along long runs."#,
                    ),
                ],
            ),
            answer: (
