                    (
                        label: "(b) One IR, two node families",
                        caption: r#"A pure gradiance-graph crate: nodes by StableId, typed ports, edges by id; a signal family (frame rate, lowers to the kernel) and a shape family (edit rate, lowers to ShapeDef); bodies and joints are reference nodes; the graph is scene content edited through graph.* operations; positions saved. Cost: a new crate, two format bumps, the canvas adapter rewritten in two briefs."#,
                    ),
                    (
                        label: "(c) The graph is the document",
                        caption: r#"Graphite's model: every body, joint and setting is a node output and the save is the graph. Cost: large; the save stops being materialized state, simulated poses need a rest/live split, every command and the undo path are rebuilt, and 3D changes how the whole document evaluates."#,
                    ),
                ],
            ),
